  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. Every one of the 18 listed sites is still present; the 3 \"fixed already\" sites are gone. Sites relocated by anchor phrase, not line.\n\nFIXED (confirmed absent today): ADR-0016 \"eventually calls socket.send\" / \"Amendment (INV-fotav)\" / \"originally recorded the opposite\"; ADR-0046 \"not the one predicted here\".\n\nSTILL PRESENT, line now: 0005 L8, 0010 L460, 0014 L9, 0015 L9, 0016 L334 (was 331), 0017 L9 + L629 (was 586), 0018 L121, 0024 L12, 0028 L10, 0033 L13 + L15 + L110, 0034 L10, 0035 L87 + L110, 0045 L27 (was 29), 3bbb L15. The 09-29 commit a775b4d3de (\"catalogue ADRs state the final design only\") touched 0017 and 0045 but not these sites. ADR-0016's separate L105 shape is now L103, unchanged.\n\nREAD, the item's five \"clearest\" sites:\n- 0017 L620-633: TRUE instance. \"Two blockers this banner used to name are CLOSED, recorded rather than deleted\" and \"Provenance of this correction. The paragraph above previously described ... reading neither\" -- the retracted claim is restated.\n- 0010 L460: \"more permissive than originally specified\" -- the strict spec text is no longer in the ADR (no \"exact failing job\" match); a residual note, not retained wrong text.\n- 0016 L334 (\"the consumer this section originally specified\"), 0045 L27 (\"That reasoning was applied to the backend-active case\"), 3bbb L15 (\"The taxonomy as originally specified\", context about ADR-3aaa): regex hits, NOT retracted-in-place text on reading.\n- The banner sites 0005 L8, 0014 L9, 0015 L9, 0017 L9, 0018 L121, 0028 L10, 0033 L15, 0034 L10 each say the body BELOW states a superseded rule -- the excise-the-superseded-body shape; not adjudicated one by one here.\n\nNEW HITS outside the pool (same regex family, not adjudicated): 0005 L12 (\"not the one this amendment originally predicted\" -- the same shape as the excised ADR-0046 text), 0041 L74 (\"This paragraph originally named ...\"), 0043 L189 (\"This reverses the retention #9 originally asserted\"), 0012 L36, 0027 L191, 3bbb L84/L126.\nCount drift: the title's \"14 of 49 ADRs\" -- there are now 63 ADR files (+README)."  # a848
