    description: "FROM THE OWNER, 2026-08-27, on finding ADR-0016 carrying a retracted argument\nbeside the surviving conclusion:\n\n  \"even if adr-16 ultimately conveys the correct message on careful reading,\n   readers do not always read carefully! we have already established that ADRs\n   are git-tracked and as such it is perfectly fine to remove obsolete\n   information from them. this is a case in point of containing both the\n   information and the disinformation side-by-side. the solution is NOT to\n   explain the disinfo at length, the solution is to ELIMINATE THOSE WORDS.\"\n\nTHE DEFECT SHAPE. An ADR is amended, and instead of the wrong text being\nDELETED it is kept and then refuted underneath. The document then contains the\nclaim and its refutation at equal typographic weight, and a reader who stops\nearly leaves with the wrong one. AGENTS.md already states the rule this\nviolates -- \"excise-the-superseded-BODY (don't leave stale text behind a\nmissable banner)\" -- so this is drift from a written rule, not a new policy.\n\nALREADY EXCISED (confirmed absent 2026-09-30): ADR-0016 \"Why static analysis\ncan answer this\" (the \"requests.get() eventually calls socket.send()\"\nparagraph and its \"Amendment (INV-fotav)\" refutation); ADR-0016\nmodule_completeness (\"This paragraph originally recorded the opposite\");\nADR-0046 Consequences (\"the reason is not the one predicted here\").\n\nCANDIDATE POOL, current lines at dev 134a06d505 (63 ADRs). A regex over\ndocs/adr/*.md for retraction-in-place language is a finder, not a judgement.\n\n  CONFIRMED INSTANCE, on reading:\n    0017 L620-633 -- \"Two blockers this banner used to name are CLOSED,\n      recorded rather than deleted\" and \"Provenance of this correction. The\n      paragraph above previously described ...\" restating the retracted claim.\n\n  BANNER OVER A SUPERSEDED BODY (each says the text BELOW states a superseded\n  rule -- the excise-the-superseded-body shape; not yet judged one by one):\n    0005 L8, 0014 L9, 0015 L9, 0017 L9, 0018 L121, 0028 L10, 0033 L15, 0034 L10.\n\n  NOT JUDGED: 0024 L12, 0033 L13 + L110, 0035 L87 + L110. An amendment that\n  only ADDS a ruling is correct and stays.\n\n  READ, NOT THIS DEFECT:\n    0010 L460 -- \"more permissive than originally specified\": the original\n      strict spec is no longer in the ADR; a residual note, not retained text.\n    0016 L334 (\"the consumer this section originally specified\"), 0045 L27\n      (\"That reasoning was applied ...\"), 3bbb L15 (\"The taxonomy as\n      originally specified\", context about ADR-3aaa) -- regex hits only.\n\n  NEW HITS, not in the original pool, unjudged: 0005 L12 (\"not the one this\n  amendment originally predicted\" -- the same shape as the excised ADR-0046\n  text), 0041 L74 (\"This paragraph originally named ...\"), 0043 L189 (\"This\n  reverses the retention #9 originally asserted\"), 0012 L36, 0027 L191,\n  3bbb L84 + L126.\n\nA SECOND, DISTINCT SHAPE, DO NOT FOLD: ADR-0016 L103 corrects a MISREADING of\nthe ADR by others (\"This ADR's prohibition was read twice as forbidding any\nbash io_primitives catalogue, and that reading is wrong\") rather than retracting\nthe ADR's own text. Deleting it would lose a real clarification; the fix there\nis to make the prohibition unambiguous where it is STATED. Different remedy,\nsame audit.\n\nWHAT DONE LOOKS LIKE: every site read and either excised or justified in the\nitem, and -- worth considering, not assumed -- a check that keeps it from\nrecurring, since the rule already existed in AGENTS.md and drifted anyway.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 1797
