  message: "WORKED 2026-09-30 (concurrent run). Branch jgstern-agent/docs/fubom-adr-retracted-text (local, not pushed), 3 commits on 8cfcab7b07: 03ba16091a, c2c5b9f8d4, 8c7a9c1762. 21 ADR files, +247/-447. Docs only; no code, no generated files. Targeted smart-test: 571 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed (27 test files, incl. tests/test_adr_supersession_symmetry.py and tests/test_adr_readme_index_sync.py).\n\nEVERY POOL SITE, verdict:\n- 0017 L620-633 (confirmed): excised; the walk's keying + sink test stated positively.\n- Banner sites: 0005 L8 (+L12) excised, rows now key on rank_score; 0014 L9 rewritten (bodies were already pointers; the banner/table restated the falsified \"survives renames\" rationale); 0015 L9 + migration-window section removed (FALSE: ADR-0038 rulings 2/3/4 shipped), dest_access_mode examples and the would_admit_dst_reader trigger removed, §7 excised to a pointer; 0017 L9 rewritten; 0018 L121 + original-design table replaced by the per-session state; 0028 L10 removed (redundant with the existing pointer); 0033 L15 folded into §3/Phase 3 (ratchet stated as the design); 0034 L10 removed, item 5 + Edge.id bullet state the shipped checks.\n- 0024 L12: OQ1 body still said \"leave as-is\" and listed read_write; now resolved by ADR-0038. 0033 L13 folded into invariant (a); L110 is an addition (kept, relabelled; stale 0.1 example fixed). 0035 L87/L110 add rulings (kept); their stale \"5b deferred\" claims removed.\n- 0010 L460: the premise check called this not-the-defect because \"the strict spec is no longer in the ADR\". WRONG: L314/L317 still said \"exact prefix required\". Both now state the shipped any-fix(job-*) check.\n- 0016 L334: one word (\"originally\"). 0045 L27, 3bbb L15, 0012 L36: read, not this defect, unchanged.\n- New hits: 0041 L74, 3bbb L84/L95/L126, 0043 L189, 0027 L191 all rewritten to state the rule/current state.\n- 0016 L103 (distinct shape): the prohibition is now unambiguous where stated (rows classifying a LAUNCHED program); the misreading note and its gap measurement were also stale (io_primitives/bash.yaml catalogues redirects), and \"a bash catalogue is still not the right answer\" contradicted the shipped catalogue.\n\nSAME SHAPE OUTSIDE THE POOL, fixed: 0012 L14 \"do not ingest\" banner; 0013 amendment said the OS-enforcement claim was \"corrected in place\" but five body sites still made it (Config Protection, security guarantee, 3 rejected-proposal rows, a Consequences bullet, mode 644 vs shipped 0444); 0017 [Invalidated by ADR-0037] / Correction / [Superseded by ADR-0038] markers and a §3a sentence saying False and None \"are the same event\" under a banner saying removal was granted -- and the \"re-key on dst_ref\" those markers promised was measured and closed wont_do (WI-lonad), so the string-parse machinery IS the design; 0037 L7/L60/L91 said consumers stop string-parsing dst / dst_ref 100%, contradicting its own sentinel exception; 0023 six-field key under a SUPERSEDED banner; 0035 reading note + §5 \"deferred v7\" (v7 shipped per its own §6); 0043 §6 table flagged non-authoritative and §6.1 struck rows -- the live code has sub-steps 6c/7/7a/7b/7c the ADR never listed; 0018 dedup default stated as 50K/100000 (code: 200000).\n\nJUDGED KEEP: 0027 L10 and 0028 Migration banner (prospective plans with DONE markers; the one divergence, the 0027 enum, fixed); 0036 Enforcement banner (pending design, not a retraction -- its stale \"why advisory\" reason noted on WI-popak); amendments that only add a ruling.\n\nNOT CHECKED: Status lines generally (0019/0020/0022/0039 carry narrative); whole-ADR reads (I read each hit's region plus what it pointed at); phrases outside the regex families used. A regex is a finder: most fixes here came from reading, not from a marker.\n\nFILED: WI-zogop (Symbol.kind enum never re-closed after Phase 4b; generator text cites removed emit sites), WI-pimud (decide on a docs/adr retained-text gate). Notes on WI-popak, WI-tuban."  # b0a3
